    "legacy_save_warning": "PowerPoint warned that slide 2 video, slide 5 SVG, slide 6 3D model, and slides 7-8 charts would be saved as pictures in the legacy derivative; the warning was accepted.",
    "known_reader_boundaries": [
      "litchi-pptx::media_parts::load_slide_media rejects slide 2 with Invalid(unsupported p14:media child 'extLst') before it can expose the native caption track; the media relationship rId2 and track relationship rId4 are present and valid in the package.",
      "litchi-pptx::Slide::model3ds rejects slide 6 because PowerPoint declares the GLB content type as model/gltf.binary while the reader currently requires model/gltf-binary.",
      "litchi-pptx::Slide::chart_extensions parses slide 8's ChartEx sunburst but rejects slide 7's native waterfall subtotal syntax with Invalid(\"invalid  subtotal index\"); PowerPoint uses <cx:subtotals><cx:idx val=\"0\"/>...</cx:subtotals>.",
      "litchi-pptx::presentation::SourceBackedPresentation::images refuses slides 4, 6, 7 and 8 because the picture fallback is inside an MCE AlternateContent branch whose ownership is ambiguous; slide 5 instead refuses because a:blip has no direct r:embed or r:link and the SVG relationship is carried by asvg:svgBlip.",
      "litchi-ppt::Presentation::images fails with OfficeArt(MalformedImage { reason: resolved BLIP UID does not match the FBSE UID }) for this legacy derivative; typed external_media and ole_objects records remain readable.",
      "The source GLB is transformed by PowerPoint's native importer before being stored as model3d1.glb, and the source SVG is minified and rewritten as image4.svg; both package payloads retain their deterministic visible markers but are not byte-identical to their import assets."
    ]
  },
